Name synced sidecars the way Jellyfin reads them, and apply settings immediately

Two faults, both reported from real use.

1. Synced sidecars were invisible in Jellyfin. A sidecar has to begin with the exact media
   filename and then dot-separated fields (Film.mkv -> Film.en.sdh.srt); the synced marker was
   glued on with a hyphen, so Jellyfin could not attach the file to the episode. The marker is now
   a field: "<name>.SYNCED.<lang>.srt". Existing hyphenated files are left alone.

2. Settings could be saved and never applied, which made a worker count of 8 run as 4 and
   "replace the original" write copies. The plugin read the configuration copy from its own
   construction time. Every read now goes through SettingsSource: the settings file Jellyfin
   writes is the source of truth, re-read whenever it changes, with the in-memory copy as the
   fallback. Verified that a file round-trips workers, sync mode and VAD method, and that a
   missing or malformed file neither throws nor loses the last known settings.

For embedded tracks, "replace" and "copy" remain identical by design: the original is inside the
video and the video is never modified, so a new sidecar is always written.

Checks: 144, ALL PASS.

Version 1.1.0.38.
